const V={};
V.home=()=>`<section class="hero"><div class="two"><div><div class="kick">Investigation · Khyber Pakhtunkhwa admissions</div><h1>Open merit under threat</h1><p class="lead">KMU’s official 2026–27 table cuts ${CUTN} open-merit MBBS seats at ${NUM[CUT.length]} public colleges. The quota seats created after 2020 did not change at any college.</p><div class="by">By the Open Merit Archive · Updated 18 November 2026 · ${L.length} records, every claim graded</div><div class="stat3"><div><b>${CUTN}</b><span>open-merit MBBS seats cut across ${NUM[CUT.length]} colleges, while ${GAIN} are added at ${NUM[NGAIN]} others.</span></div><div><b>0</b><span>seats changed in the Merged Districts quota (254) and HEC project seats (91) at any MBBS college.</span></div><div><b>81</b><span>fewer open-merit BDS seats than in 2023–24: 115 now, 196 then.</span></div></div></div><aside class="pkg"><h4>In this investigation</h4><a href="/story">Read the story<span>Six steps, with the map</span></a><a href="/official">See the official tables<span>MBBS and BDS, every category, with changes</span></a><a href="/browse">Search the evidence<span>${L.length} records, each graded</span></a><a href="/network">See the connections<span>Who controls which seats</span></a><a href="/compare">Compare the years<span>Category-wise seats, 2020–27</span></a><a href="/verify">How we grade evidence<span>Method and key figures</span></a></aside></div></section>
<div class="enote"><b>About the numbers.</b> Every 2026–27 figure on this site comes from KMU’s official seat distribution, supplied on 18 November 2026. Earlier years come from KMU’s own admission policies. Insider claims are graded separately and are not treated as fact.</div>
<h2>What we found</h2><ol class="find">
<li><div><b>${CUTN} open-merit MBBS seats are cut at ${NUM[CUT.length]} colleges:</b> ${CUT.map(c=>c[1]+" "+sg(c[5]-c[4])).join(", ")}. Saidu, Gomal and Bacha Khan gain ${GAIN}, and SMDAS adds 81. <a href="/colleges">College ledger</a></div></li>
<li><div><b>The quota seats did not move.</b> Merged Districts (254) and HEC project seats (91) are identical to 2025–26 at every college. <a href="/compare">Compare the years</a></div></li>
<li><div><b>Open merit took the whole reversion.</b> At the six colleges PMDC cut back, capacity falls by ${CAP6} seats and open merit by ${CUT6}. <a href="/official">Official tables</a></div></li>
<li><div><b>Dental seats fall hardest.</b> Open-merit BDS seats are 115, down 81 from 196 in 2023–24, while the quota totals hold. <a href="/official#bds">BDS table</a></div></li>
<li><div><b>The “+${HEAD}” headline hides a fee gap.</b> 81 of the new open-merit seats are at SMDAS, where Dawn reported a fee of Rs 1.8 million a year, about 18 times the open-merit fee. <a href="/entity?id=smdas">SMDAS</a></div></li>
<li><div><b>The table shows what changed, not why.</b> PMDC’s email calls last year’s intake one-time, but nothing published says who chose to take the cut from open merit. <a href="/entity?id=email">The email</a></div></li></ol>
<h2>The network behind the cuts</h2><p class="mut">Institutions, seat categories, colleges and events, connected by what the documents say. Drag, zoom, and click any node.</p><div class="stage"><canvas id="cv" style="height:440px"></canvas></div>
<h2>Latest records</h2><div class="grid">${L.filter(e=>!(e.y=="OFF"&&e.c)&&e.y!="PORTAL").slice(-6).reverse().map(card).join("")}</div>
<h2>What our contributor claimed</h2><p class="mut">These claims came from one contributor. KMU’s official table confirms one of them; the rest are still unverified.</p>${L.filter(e=>e.y=="INTEL").map(e=>`<div class="card ec" data-id="${e.id}" style="margin:8px 0">${tag(e.g)}<b>${e.t.replace("Claim: ","")}</b></div>`).join("")}`;
